0
00:00:02,102 --> 00:00:04,438
Tyra: PREVIOUSLY ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"...

1
00:00:04,438 --> 00:00:06,974
Cassie: I WORRY ABOUT
WHAT I EAT 24-7.

2
00:00:06,974 --> 00:00:08,742
Tyra: CASSIE
REVEALED AN OBSESSION

3
00:00:08,742 --> 00:00:09,743
WITH HER BODY IMAGE...

4
00:00:09,743 --> 00:00:11,078
Cassie:
I WANT TO BE A MODEL.

5
00:00:11,078 --> 00:00:13,046
I FEEL LIKE I SHOULD
BE SKINNY.

6
00:00:13,046 --> 00:00:15,816
Tyra: AND NORELLE
STRUGGLED ON THE RUNWAY.

7
00:00:17,985 --> 00:00:19,853
Norelle: WHOA!

8
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:20,954
Audience: (gasps)

9
00:00:20,954 --> 00:00:22,089
Tyra:
WHEN KELLE FAILED AGAIN

10
00:00:22,089 --> 00:00:23,757
TO PROVE SHE WAS
PHOTOGENIC,

11
00:00:23,757 --> 00:00:25,392
SHE WAS SENT PACKING.

12
00:00:25,392 --> 00:00:27,194
EIGHT GIRLS REMAIN.

13
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:29,863
WHO WILL BE
ELIMINATED TONIGHT?

14
00:00:29,863 --> 00:00:32,766
♪♪♪

15
00:01:07,703 --> 00:01:08,068
♪♪♪

16
00:01:13,006 --> 00:01:15,008
Eva: I JUST FELL
ON THE LAVA!

17
00:01:15,008 --> 00:01:17,110
OH, MY GOD!
OH, MY GOD!

18
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:19,546
DON'T SAY THAT!

19
00:01:19,546 --> 00:01:21,181
Amanda:
LONDON BRIDGE!

20
00:01:21,181 --> 00:01:23,083
Norelle: DON'T FALL
IN THE LAVA.

21
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:24,284
Amanda:
ARE YOU A CHEERLEADER?

22
00:01:24,284 --> 00:01:26,420
Eva: OH, MY GOD!

23
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:28,355
Ann: HOW FUNNY WAS THAT,
THE LAVA?

24
00:01:28,355 --> 00:01:30,357
Cassie:
I'M JUST NOT HAVING FUN.

25
00:01:30,357 --> 00:01:31,458
I DON'T WANT TO MISS
MY FAMILY,

26
00:01:31,458 --> 00:01:33,160
AND I DON'T WANT
TO MISS MY BOYFRIEND,

27
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:35,395
BUT MY HEART IS HURTING
RIGHT NOW.

28
00:01:35,395 --> 00:01:38,999
IT'S JUST REALLY SAD, LIKE,
THERE'S A SADNESS INSIDE OF ME.

29
00:01:38,999 --> 00:01:40,300
LIFE CHANGES
IF YOU WIN THIS.

30
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:41,268
Cassie's boyfriend:
YEAH.

31
00:01:41,268 --> 00:01:43,103
Cassie: YOU HAVE
TO MOVE TO NEW YORK.

32
00:01:43,103 --> 00:01:44,938
YOU DON'T HAVE TIME FOR
A BOYFRIEND ANYMORE.

33
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:46,940
YOU DON'T HAVE TIME
TO DO ANYTHING EXCEPT WORK.

34
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,508
Cassie's boyfriend:
I MEAN, HEY,

35
00:01:48,508 --> 00:01:49,576
YOU GOTTA DO
WHAT YOU GOTTA DO.

36
00:01:49,576 --> 00:01:51,211
Cassie: WILL YOU
GO THERE WITH ME?

37
00:01:51,211 --> 00:01:52,980
Cassie's boyfriend:
AM I GONNA COME WITH YOU?

38
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:55,248
WELL, I'M NOT JUST GONNA
PICK UP AND LEAVE.

39
00:01:55,248 --> 00:01:57,417
Cassie: NO, C.J.!

40
00:01:57,417 --> 00:01:59,319
I DON'T WANT
TO LET YOU GO.

41
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:02,089
I LOVE YOU.

42
00:02:07,494 --> 00:02:09,463
Toccara: THAT CHICKEN'S
STARTING TO LOOK GOOD, THOUGH.

43
00:02:09,463 --> 00:02:10,964
Yaya: SERIOUSLY,
YOU'RE GONNA GET SICK

44
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:12,966
IF YOU JUST LEAVE IT
LIKE THAT.

45
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:14,601
Toccara: I DO
LIKE THAT ALL THE TIME.

46
00:02:14,601 --> 00:02:16,103
I MIGHT ROLL OVER IN THE MIDDLE
OF THE NIGHT AND EAT SOMETHING.

47
00:02:16,103 --> 00:02:17,270
MY MAMA EAT IN HER SLEEP.

48
00:02:17,270 --> 00:02:18,271
Yaya:
THAT'S NOT GOOD.

49
00:02:18,271 --> 00:02:20,574
Toccara: WHEN SHE BE ASLEEP,
SHE BE LIKE...

50
00:02:22,909 --> 00:02:24,845
I LOVE MYSELF.
I LOVE MY SHAPE.

51
00:02:24,845 --> 00:02:26,146
I LOVE MY CURVES.

52
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:28,482
SOME PEOPLE THINK
THAT AMERICA'S "NOT READY"

53
00:02:28,482 --> 00:02:30,317
FOR A PLUS-SIZED MODEL.

54
00:02:30,317 --> 00:02:32,052
I'M HERE
TO BREAK THAT NORM.

55
00:02:32,052 --> 00:02:33,854
I WANT TO BE THE FIRST
BLACK PLUS-SIZED MODEL

56
00:02:33,854 --> 00:02:35,922
TO BE ON THE COVER
OF 20 MAGAZINES.

57
00:02:35,922 --> 00:02:37,624
I DON'T WANT
TO STAY IN MY CATEGORY.

58
00:02:37,624 --> 00:02:39,960
I WANT TO GO INTO
THE "STRAIGHT SIDE."

59
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:41,528
Norelle: I WISH
I WAS MORE LIKE TOCCARA.

60
00:02:41,528 --> 00:02:43,063
SHE'S FABULOUS.

61
00:02:43,063 --> 00:02:44,231
SHE HAS CONFIDENCE
IN HERSELF.

62
00:02:44,231 --> 00:02:46,033
CAN YOU SEE IT?

63
00:02:46,033 --> 00:02:48,168
Ann: EVERYONE HAS THAT,
LIKE, I HAVE THAT.

64
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:50,037
Norelle: MY STOMACH
HAS, LIKE, A LITTLE PUDGE.

65
00:02:50,037 --> 00:02:51,605
I WOULD LIKE IT
TO BE MORE ABBY,

66
00:02:51,605 --> 00:02:53,306
AND I STILL HAVE
A LITTLE BIT OF FLABBY.

67
00:02:55,275 --> 00:02:57,878
(telephone ringing)

68
00:02:57,878 --> 00:03:00,080
- Yaya: HELLO.
- Tyra: Hi, it's Tyra.

69
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,915
All right, I need you to get
everybody together, okay?

70
00:03:01,915 --> 00:03:04,317
Because you guys are gonna
meet me for a little challenge.

71
00:03:04,317 --> 00:03:06,420
Now you need to wear
some comfortable shoes,

72
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:08,221
but bring some
high heels, too.

73
00:03:08,221 --> 00:03:10,590
Yaya:
GOOD MORNING, HELLO!

74
00:03:10,590 --> 00:03:11,591
I JUST GOT A CALL
FROM TYRA.

75
00:03:11,591 --> 00:03:13,460
WE HAVE TO DRESS
LIKE WE'RE GOING TO PANEL

76
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,462
AND BRING COMFORTABLE SHOES.

77
00:03:15,462 --> 00:03:17,164
TYRA JUST CALLED.

78
00:03:17,164 --> 00:03:19,166
WAKE UP.

79
00:03:19,166 --> 00:03:21,301
Norelle: WE WERE TOLD
TO BRING FLATS AND HEELS.

80
00:03:21,301 --> 00:03:22,402
WE DIDN'T KNOW WHY.

81
00:03:22,402 --> 00:03:25,238
Toccara: SHE'S WALKING
OUT THE DOOR.

82
00:03:27,074 --> 00:03:29,609
♪♪♪

83
00:03:31,311 --> 00:03:32,345
Tyra: HI, EVERYBODY.

84
00:03:32,345 --> 00:03:33,580
Eva: HEY, TYRA.

85
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:35,015
Tyra: SO YOU GUYS HAVE BEEN
WORKING REALLY HARD

86
00:03:35,015 --> 00:03:36,483
FOR THE LAST
COUPLE OF WEEKS.

87
00:03:36,483 --> 00:03:38,919
YOU'VE BEEN WORKING WITH SOME
OF THE TOP PHOTOGRAPHERS,

88
00:03:38,919 --> 00:03:40,987
BUT PEOPLE
DON'T KNOW YOU EXIST.

89
00:03:40,987 --> 00:03:44,357
NOW IT'S TIME TO SEND YOU OUT
TO THE SHARKS.

90
00:03:44,357 --> 00:03:47,360
YOU'RE GONNA EXPERIENCE
A DAY IN THE LIFE OF A MODEL

91
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:50,197
GOING ON GO-SEES DURING
FASHION WEEK.

92
00:03:50,197 --> 00:03:52,866
A GO-SEE MEANS YOU
JUST GO SEE THE CLIENT

93
00:03:52,866 --> 00:03:55,902
TO LET THEM KNOW THAT
YOU ARE ALIVE,

94
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:58,038
SO WE HAVE PUT TOGETHER
PORTFOLIOS HERE.

95
00:03:58,038 --> 00:04:00,407
Girls: (squealing)

96
00:04:00,407 --> 00:04:02,008
Eva: TYRA GAVE US
OUR PORTFOLIOS,

97
00:04:02,008 --> 00:04:05,078
OUR BEST PHOTOS THAT
WE HAVE TAKEN THUS FAR.

98
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:05,912
I WAS SO STOKED.

99
00:04:07,314 --> 00:04:09,216
IT WAS JUST SO EXCITING,

100
00:04:09,216 --> 00:04:11,418
'CAUSE IT MAKES YOU FEEL LIKE,
"HEY, I'M MODELING.

101
00:04:11,418 --> 00:04:13,420
I CAN DO THIS, TOO."

102
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:16,389
Ann: I'M THE ONE THAT HAS,
LIKE, THE WORST PORTFOLIO.

103
00:04:16,389 --> 00:04:19,024
Nolé: YOUR BODY LANGUAGE
IS NOT GOOD.

104
00:04:19,024 --> 00:04:21,428
Tyra: OUT OF ALL THE GIRLS,
YOU WERE THE WORST.

105
00:04:21,428 --> 00:04:24,097
Ann: LAST WEEK I WAS IN
THE BOTTOM TWO FOR ELIMINATION.

106
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:26,399
Tyra: PRETTY GIRL,
NOT PHOTOGENIC.

107
00:04:26,399 --> 00:04:29,136
Ann: BUT I FEEL
GOOD ABOUT GO-SEES,

108
00:04:29,136 --> 00:04:31,204
BECAUSE IT'S IN PERSON,
AND IT'S NOT PICTURES.

109
00:04:31,204 --> 00:04:35,075
THEY'LL LIKE ME IN PERSON,
AND I'M PRETTY IN PERSON.

110
00:04:35,075 --> 00:04:36,943
Tyra: YOU'RE GONNA BE JUDGED
ON OVERALL LOOKS.

111
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:39,212
WE KNOW THIS IS
THE MODELING INDUSTRY,

112
00:04:39,212 --> 00:04:40,213
SO IT IS ABOUT THE PHYSICAL.

113
00:04:40,213 --> 00:04:42,449
YOU'RE GONNA BE JUDGED
ON YOUR WALK.

114
00:04:42,449 --> 00:04:45,986
YOU'RE ALSO GONNA BE
JUDGED ON YOUR PERSONALITY.

115
00:04:45,986 --> 00:04:49,589
OF COURSE, WHOEVER GETS
THE MOST PRAISE

116
00:04:49,589 --> 00:04:52,292
GETS AN AMAZING PRIZE--
A RACK OF CLOTHES...

117
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,426
Eva: OH, MY...

118
00:04:53,426 --> 00:04:55,562
Tyra: ...FROM EACH DESIGNER
THAT YOU SEE TODAY.

119
00:04:55,562 --> 00:04:58,431
THESE GIRLS
ARE SO LUCKY.

120
00:04:58,431 --> 00:05:00,667
I SET UP FOR THEM TO HAVE
GO-SEES WITH FIVE

121
00:05:00,667 --> 00:05:02,536
OF THE TOP DESIGNERS
IN NEW YORK CITY--

122
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:06,473
DIANE VON FURSTENBERG,

123
00:05:10,410 --> 00:05:11,878
NANETTE LEPORE,

124
00:05:14,147 --> 00:05:15,315
MARC BOUWER,

125
00:05:17,918 --> 00:05:19,119
CYNTHIA ROWLEY

126
00:05:21,955 --> 00:05:23,924
AND NICOLE MILLER.

127
00:05:30,363 --> 00:05:32,165
Ann: GOING TO THE GO-SEES,
I KNOW I HAVE TO MAKE

128
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:34,935
THE RIGHT IMPRESSION,
YOU KNOW, COME ACROSS

129
00:05:34,935 --> 00:05:36,570
AS BEING SOMEONE THAT
THEY WANT TO WORK WITH.

130
00:05:36,570 --> 00:05:37,571
Nicole Miller:
I'M NICOLE.

131
00:05:37,571 --> 00:05:39,072
Ann: I'M ANN.
NICE TO MEET YOU.

132
00:05:39,072 --> 00:05:40,106
Nicole Miller:
LIKE YOUR T-SHIRT.

133
00:05:40,106 --> 00:05:41,474
- IT'S CUTE.
- Ann: THANK YOU.

134
00:05:41,474 --> 00:05:42,943
IT'S DIFFERENT BEING
IN NEW YORK,

135
00:05:42,943 --> 00:05:44,578
'CAUSE I'M SO NOT USED TO,
LIKE, FASHION AND STUFF.

136
00:05:44,578 --> 00:05:46,079
Nicole Miller:
WELL, WE'RE CASTING FOR

137
00:05:46,079 --> 00:05:48,148
OUR MILLER GIRL
FASHION SHOW,

138
00:05:48,148 --> 00:05:51,918
SO WE WANT SOMEBODY WITH
A REALLY YOUNG, PEPPY LOOK.

139
00:05:51,918 --> 00:05:53,486
SO WE'RE GONNA PUT
AN OUTFIT ON YOU,

140
00:05:53,486 --> 00:05:55,255
AND THEN WE'RE
GONNA SEE HOW YOU WALK.

141
00:05:55,255 --> 00:05:56,289
Ann:
SOUNDS GOOD.

142
00:05:56,289 --> 00:05:58,625
Woman: GREAT LOOKS,
GOOD PERSONALITY.

143
00:05:58,625 --> 00:06:01,595
♪♪♪

144
00:06:07,567 --> 00:06:08,835
Nicole Miller: SO HOW'D YOU
GET THE NAME YAYA?

145
00:06:08,835 --> 00:06:10,237
THAT'S SO UNUSUAL.

146
00:06:10,237 --> 00:06:12,205
Yaya: IT'S ACTUALLY
REALLY COMMON IN WEST AFRICA.

147
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:14,140
Nicole Miller:
OKAY.

148
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:16,376
Toccara: NICOLE MILLER,
HER CLOTHES ARE GREAT.

149
00:06:16,376 --> 00:06:19,112
THEY FIT ME, AND I FELT
VERY WONDERFUL IN THEM.

150
00:06:19,112 --> 00:06:21,381
Norelle: HI.

151
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:22,382
Nicole Miller:
WHERE ARE YOU FROM?

152
00:06:22,382 --> 00:06:24,184
Norelle: CALIFORNIA,
ORANGE COUNTY.

153
00:06:24,184 --> 00:06:26,186
I DON'T THINK I'M THE
MOST BEAUTIFUL GIRL HERE.

154
00:06:26,186 --> 00:06:29,022
LIKE, I'M SO, LIKE, FUNNY
AND RETARDED, LIKE, DORKY GIRL.

155
00:06:29,022 --> 00:06:30,257
Nicole Miller: YOU'VE
NEVER DONE ANY MODELING?

156
00:06:30,257 --> 00:06:31,524
AH.

157
00:06:31,524 --> 00:06:33,460
Norelle: AND I JUST HOPE
THAT THEY SEE, LIKE,

158
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:34,861
SOME POTENTIAL IN ME.

159
00:06:34,861 --> 00:06:36,897
Nicole Miller: NO, NO, NO,
NO, STOP RIGHT THERE.

160
00:06:36,897 --> 00:06:40,066
MORE LIKE
AN ASSERTIVE WALK, OKAY?

161
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:44,437
Amanda: I WANTED
TO SLAP MYSELF

162
00:06:44,437 --> 00:06:46,840
WHEN I SAW THAT
ALL THE OTHER GIRLS

163
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:49,175
HAVE HIGH HEELS WITH 'EM,
AND I DON'T.

164
00:06:49,175 --> 00:06:51,411
Eva: YOU OF ALL PEOPLE
GONNA FORGET YOUR SHOES.

165
00:06:51,411 --> 00:06:53,847
Amanda: I JUST
WASN'T THINKING.

166
00:06:53,847 --> 00:06:55,215
Norelle: AMANDA
DIDN'T HAVE SHOES,

167
00:06:55,215 --> 00:06:56,616
SO I LET HER
BORROW MY SHOES.

168
00:06:56,616 --> 00:06:58,018
Amanda:
I GOTTA WEAR SHOES

169
00:06:58,018 --> 00:06:59,619
THAT WERE ONE AND A HALF
SIZES TOO SMALL.

170
00:07:02,155 --> 00:07:04,524
MY WALK'S VERY UNEVEN
AND KINDA LIKE,

171
00:07:04,524 --> 00:07:08,061
SWAYED TO AND FRO.

172
00:07:08,061 --> 00:07:09,396
Nicole Miller:
OKAY.

173
00:07:09,396 --> 00:07:11,364
Amanda: RIGHT NOW
I NEED TO DO SOMETHING

174
00:07:11,364 --> 00:07:13,533
THAT MAKES MY CONFIDENCE
HIGHER.

175
00:07:13,533 --> 00:07:15,969
Ann:
AMANDA FORGOT HER SHOES,

176
00:07:15,969 --> 00:07:19,839
SO SHE NEEDED TO RUN
TO THE STORE,

177
00:07:19,839 --> 00:07:21,875
AND, OF COURSE,
WE ALL WANTED TO GO.

178
00:07:21,875 --> 00:07:23,109
WE WANTED TO LOOK
AT SHOES.

179
00:07:23,109 --> 00:07:27,380
AND SO AMANDA WENT,
EVA WENT, I WENT,

180
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:29,082
TOCCARA WENT
AND CASSIE WENT.

181
00:07:29,082 --> 00:07:32,185
Amanda: 7 1/2, TALL STILETTO,
BRIGHT COLOR.

182
00:07:32,185 --> 00:07:33,253
Ann: I LOVE SHOES.

183
00:07:33,253 --> 00:07:34,487
Cassie: AND IT WAS
ONLY 15 MINUTES

184
00:07:34,487 --> 00:07:35,989
BEFORE OUR NEXT GO-SEE.

185
00:07:38,158 --> 00:07:40,961
♪♪♪

186
00:07:43,096 --> 00:07:44,230
Yaya:
THIS IS A COMPETITION,

187
00:07:44,230 --> 00:07:47,334
AND SO NOT ALL OF US
WERE RUNNING AROUND.

188
00:07:47,334 --> 00:07:49,469
I UNDERSTAND IF ONE PERSON
NEEDS TO GET A PAIR OF SHOES,

189
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:52,272
BUT THE FACT THAT IT TURNED
INTO A FIELD TRIP,

190
00:07:52,272 --> 00:07:54,574
I WAS NOT HAPPY.

191
00:07:54,574 --> 00:07:55,508
Eva:
WHAT TIME YOU GOT?

192
00:07:55,508 --> 00:07:57,110
Ann: WE HAD 15 MINUTES,

193
00:07:57,110 --> 00:07:59,512
AND I THINK WE WERE THERE
A LITTLE LONGER.

194
00:07:59,512 --> 00:08:02,415
♪♪♪

195
00:08:07,387 --> 00:08:09,089
Toccara:
WHERE'S THE CAR?

196
00:08:09,089 --> 00:08:12,525
OUR VEHICLES
HAD LEFT US, GONE.

197
00:08:12,525 --> 00:08:14,327
GONE, JUST GONE.

198
00:08:14,327 --> 00:08:15,495
(horn honks)

199
00:08:15,495 --> 00:08:16,496
Cassie: OUR VAN IS GONE,

200
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:19,566
AND WE DON'T KNOW WHERE
OUR NEXT GO-SEE IS.

201
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:24,871
Ann: WE WENT BACK UP
TO NICOLE MILLER.

202
00:08:24,871 --> 00:08:26,906
Cassie: HI, DO YOU GUYS
HAVE OUR ITINERARY?

203
00:08:26,906 --> 00:08:27,974
- I MEAN, THEY LEFT US.
- Eva: DO YOU?

204
00:08:27,974 --> 00:08:29,576
Cassie: DO YOU KNOW ANYWHERE
ABOUT WHERE WE'RE GOING?

205
00:08:29,576 --> 00:08:32,379
Woman: GO TO WEST 39th
BETWEEN 7th AND 8th.

206
00:08:32,379 --> 00:08:33,947
Woman: EVA, DO YOU
WANT US TO HELP YOU?

207
00:08:33,947 --> 00:08:35,081
Eva: PLEASE!

208
00:08:35,081 --> 00:08:36,383
Ann: EVA!

209
00:08:36,383 --> 00:08:38,183
- Toccara: EVERYONE IS GO--
- Ann: I'M NOT LEAVING EVA!

210
00:08:38,183 --> 00:08:39,586
Toccara: WHAT IS IT?

211
00:08:39,586 --> 00:08:41,287
Ann:
DAMN, DON'T RIP IT!

212
00:08:41,287 --> 00:08:43,023
Toccara: 214!

213
00:08:43,023 --> 00:08:45,959
Cassie: YOU GUYS LEFT ME!
WHAT THE HELL?

214
00:08:45,959 --> 00:08:47,894
Toccara:
GET OUT OF THE WAY!

215
00:08:57,252 --> 00:09:01,306
♪♪♪

216
00:09:01,306 --> 00:09:02,307
Cassie: OUR VAN IS GONE,

217
00:09:02,307 --> 00:09:05,243
AND WE DON'T KNOW WHERE
OUR NEXT GO-SEE IS.

218
00:09:05,243 --> 00:09:06,444
NONE OF US
WERE NEW YORKERS.

219
00:09:06,444 --> 00:09:07,445
EVERYONE WAS FREAKING OUT.

220
00:09:07,445 --> 00:09:08,647
Eva: THEY LEFT US.

221
00:09:08,647 --> 00:09:10,549
DO YOU KNOW ANYWHERE
ABOUT WHERE WE'RE GOING?

222
00:09:10,549 --> 00:09:11,983
Woman: GO TO WEST 39th.

223
00:09:11,983 --> 00:09:15,187
Yaya: NICOLE, NORELLE
AND I ARRIVED FIRST,

224
00:09:15,187 --> 00:09:17,322
AND WE WERE WAITING
IN THE LOBBY FOR THEM.

225
00:09:17,322 --> 00:09:19,424
I FELT LIKE A HALF AN HOUR
WENT BY.

226
00:09:21,126 --> 00:09:23,461
Cassie: WE WERE 20 MINUTES
LATE TO NANETTE LEPORE.

227
00:09:23,461 --> 00:09:24,963
Eva: UP, I'M GOING UP.

228
00:09:24,963 --> 00:09:27,065
Amanda:
WE'RE ALREADY LATE.

229
00:09:27,065 --> 00:09:28,934
Cassie: COME ON, COME ON,
COME ON, WE'RE IN SUCH A HURRY.

230
00:09:28,934 --> 00:09:33,004
Woman: HI,
WELCOME TO NANETTE LEPORE.

231
00:09:33,004 --> 00:09:34,406
Man: MODELS.

232
00:09:34,406 --> 00:09:36,074
Yaya: HI!

233
00:09:36,074 --> 00:09:38,076
Nanette: NOW I HAVE
TO TELL EVERYONE

234
00:09:38,076 --> 00:09:39,711
THAT YOU'RE
20 MINUTES LATE.

235
00:09:39,711 --> 00:09:41,479
I'M VERY UPSET.

236
00:09:41,479 --> 00:09:43,481
YOU REALLY HAVE TO MAKE
YOUR DEADLINES

237
00:09:43,481 --> 00:09:46,418
IF YOU'RE SERIOUS ABOUT
HAVING A CAREER IN MODELING.

238
00:09:46,418 --> 00:09:48,353
SO WE'RE GONNA BRING YOU
BACK IN ONE AT A TIME

239
00:09:48,353 --> 00:09:50,722
AND JUST PLEASE REMEMBER,
IF YOU HAVE TO MEET

240
00:09:50,722 --> 00:09:53,024
ANY KIND OF DEADLINE
WHERE I'M INVOLVED,

241
00:09:53,024 --> 00:09:54,593
PLEASE RESPECT IT
FROM NOW ON.

242
00:09:54,593 --> 00:09:55,594
Man: WHOSE FAULT WAS IT?

243
00:09:55,594 --> 00:09:56,595
Eva: THERE WAS FIVE OF US.

244
00:09:56,595 --> 00:09:58,096
Toccara: THERE WAS FIVE
OF US BUT...

245
00:09:58,096 --> 00:09:59,731
Amanda: I'LL TAKE
ALL RESPONSIBILITY.

246
00:09:59,731 --> 00:10:02,567
I DON'T THINK SHE UNDERSTOOD
THE FACT THAT IT WASN'T JUST ME.

247
00:10:04,603 --> 00:10:06,338
Nanette: SO WHAT SIZE
ARE YOU?

248
00:10:06,338 --> 00:10:08,473
Amanda:
UM, THESE ARE 25s.

249
00:10:08,473 --> 00:10:13,144
I FELT TAKING RESPONSIBILITY
WOULD GET ME SOME POINTS,

250
00:10:13,144 --> 00:10:16,348
BUT IT JUST MADE HER
REALLY DISLIKE ME.

251
00:10:16,348 --> 00:10:17,983
Nanette:
OKAY, SO AMANDA.

252
00:10:17,983 --> 00:10:19,618
I GAVE HER "HIPPYISH"
FOR PERSONAL STYLE,

253
00:10:19,618 --> 00:10:21,186
A LITTLE
BIKER MEETS HIPPY.

254
00:10:21,186 --> 00:10:22,654
Man: SHE'S ALSO REALLY
LONG-WAISTED.

255
00:10:22,654 --> 00:10:24,389
SHE'S GOT REALLY SHORT LEGS.

256
00:10:24,389 --> 00:10:25,190
Nanette: POOR THING.

257
00:10:25,190 --> 00:10:26,524
NICOLE.

258
00:10:26,524 --> 00:10:27,993
SHE LOOKS LIKE
SHE'S GOT IT ALMOST.

259
00:10:27,993 --> 00:10:29,527
Man: YEAH.

260
00:10:29,527 --> 00:10:31,463
EVA, I FIND SOMETHING

261
00:10:31,463 --> 00:10:33,531
A LITTLE BIT PIGGY
ABOUT HER NOSE.

262
00:10:33,531 --> 00:10:35,100
Nanette: I THOUGHT
SHE WAS THE MOST STRIKING

263
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:37,369
WHEN WE SAW THE WHOLE
GROUP TOGETHER.

264
00:10:37,369 --> 00:10:38,570
Man: CASSIE.

265
00:10:38,570 --> 00:10:40,605
Nanette: SHE'S GOT
A CUTE, YOUNG LOOK.

266
00:10:40,605 --> 00:10:41,506
SHE MIGHT BE A LITTLE BIT...

267
00:10:41,506 --> 00:10:42,941
Man: HIPPY?

268
00:10:42,941 --> 00:10:44,376
Nanette: SHE'S NOT EXACTLY
A SIZE 2.

269
00:10:44,376 --> 00:10:45,644
THAT'S REALLY PRETTY.

270
00:10:45,644 --> 00:10:47,078
Man: NORELLE.

271
00:10:47,078 --> 00:10:49,414
I ACTUALLY THINK SHE LOOKS
BETTER IN HER PICTURES.

272
00:10:49,414 --> 00:10:52,250
ANN, BE A LITTLE BIT
ALIVE IN YOUR FACE.

273
00:10:52,250 --> 00:10:53,251
LIKE THAT.

274
00:10:53,251 --> 00:10:55,220
Nanette: YEAH, THAT'S GOOD,
THAT'S GOOD.

275
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:56,288
Man: SO MUCH BETTER.

276
00:10:56,288 --> 00:10:57,355
Yaya: JUST TO LET YOU KNOW,
THREE OF US WERE HERE

277
00:10:57,355 --> 00:10:58,690
WAITING IN THE LOBBY
FOR A HALF AN HOUR.

278
00:10:58,690 --> 00:11:00,091
Nanette: I KNOW.

279
00:11:00,091 --> 00:11:01,359
Yaya: BUT WE DO REALLY
WANT TO BE HERE.

280
00:11:01,359 --> 00:11:02,560
Nanette: I KNOW. I KNOW
THAT YOU WERE ON TIME.

281
00:11:02,560 --> 00:11:03,595
Yaya: OKAY.

282
00:11:03,595 --> 00:11:05,030
Man: SHE'S CUTE.

283
00:11:05,030 --> 00:11:07,432
Nanette: SO SHE GETS
THE ADORABLE.

284
00:11:07,432 --> 00:11:08,533
Toccara: I'M
A FULL-FIGURED MODEL.

285
00:11:08,533 --> 00:11:10,001
I'M GONNA BE THE FIRST BLACK
PLUS-SIZED SUPERMODEL

286
00:11:10,001 --> 00:11:11,303
IN THE WORLD.

287
00:11:11,303 --> 00:11:13,238
Nanette: SHE GETS, LIKE,
DOUBLE STARS HERE

288
00:11:13,238 --> 00:11:14,306
FOR PERSONALITY.

289
00:11:14,306 --> 00:11:15,707
Man: SHE'S GOTTA,
LIKE, BREAK GROUND

290
00:11:15,707 --> 00:11:18,343
IF SHE WANTS TO DO SOMETHING
IN MAINSTREAM FASHION,

291
00:11:18,343 --> 00:11:19,644
WHICH IS NOT EASY
GROUND TO BREAK.

292
00:11:19,644 --> 00:11:22,180
Toccara: WHAT SIZE SHIRT
IS THIS?

293
00:11:22,180 --> 00:11:24,282
OKAY, SORRY.

294
00:11:24,282 --> 00:11:25,283
Nanette: WE DIDN'T HAVE
YOUR SIZE.

295
00:11:25,283 --> 00:11:27,652
Toccara:
IT'S ALL RIGHT. I'M SORRY.

296
00:11:27,652 --> 00:11:29,187
THERE'S THESE CLOTHES
ON THESE RACKS,

297
00:11:29,187 --> 00:11:30,588
AND ALL THE GIRLS,
THEY CAN PROBABLY FIT

298
00:11:30,588 --> 00:11:32,157
EVERYTHING ON THERE,
YOU KNOW?

299
00:11:32,157 --> 00:11:35,026
THEY BARELY FIND
ANYTHING THAT CAN FIT ME.

300
00:11:35,026 --> 00:11:37,228
MY BREASTS LOOK OKAY?

301
00:11:37,228 --> 00:11:40,332
Man: SHE WAS BUSTING OUT
OF THAT JACKET.

302
00:11:40,332 --> 00:11:42,600
Nanette: AND THAT WOULD BE
THE BIGGEST SIZE WE CUT.

303
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:43,969
- Man: RIGHT.
- Nanette: WHAT ARE YOU
GONNA DO?

304
00:11:43,969 --> 00:11:44,970
Man: WHAT ARE WE GONNA DO?

305
00:11:44,970 --> 00:11:47,038
Toccara: IT IS
A FRUSTRATING THING

306
00:11:47,038 --> 00:11:50,475
THAT THEY DON'T HAVE
MY SIZE.

307
00:11:50,475 --> 00:11:53,378
♪♪♪

308
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:59,084
Diane: JUST WEAR THE DRESS
AND LOOK BEAUTIFUL AND EASY.

309
00:12:02,620 --> 00:12:04,122
Diane: TURN AROUND.

310
00:12:04,122 --> 00:12:05,657
Eva: IT'S BASICALLY
A COMPETITION.

311
00:12:05,657 --> 00:12:07,125
THE PERSON
WITH THE MOST POINTS

312
00:12:07,125 --> 00:12:09,661
WILL WIN A RACK OF CLOTHES
FROM THE DESIGNER.

313
00:12:09,661 --> 00:12:11,429
Diane:
WHEN I CAST A SHOW,

314
00:12:11,429 --> 00:12:17,068
ILIKE THE GIRLS TO HAVE THEIR
OWN PERSONALITY, IN A SENSE.

315
00:12:17,068 --> 00:12:19,637
AND OF COURSE,
THEY MUST KNOW HOW TO WALK.

316
00:12:19,637 --> 00:12:21,239
Norelle: I AM PROUD
OF MYSELF.

317
00:12:21,239 --> 00:12:22,340
I DIDN'T FALL,
AND I DIDN'T SLIP.

318
00:12:22,340 --> 00:12:24,009
Diane:
WHY ARE YOU SMILING?

319
00:12:24,009 --> 00:12:25,010
Norelle:
'CAUSE I'M HAPPY.

320
00:12:25,010 --> 00:12:26,044
Diane: OKAY.

321
00:12:26,044 --> 00:12:28,613
SHE DOESN'T WALK
THAT GREAT.

322
00:12:28,613 --> 00:12:30,281
Woman: IT'S HARD
FOR THEM TO WALK.

323
00:12:30,281 --> 00:12:31,716
Diane: YEAH, BUT EVEN
THE REAL MODELS CAN'T WALK.

324
00:12:31,716 --> 00:12:33,551
OKAY, SO DO WE
HAVE ANYTHING?

325
00:12:35,353 --> 00:12:36,488
UH, GIVE HER BLACK.

326
00:12:36,488 --> 00:12:38,156
IS IT WORKING?

327
00:12:38,156 --> 00:12:41,693
TOCCARA, SHE WOULD BE
A GOOD MODEL FOR PEOPLE

328
00:12:41,693 --> 00:12:44,062
WHO WOULD WANT THAT KIND
OF A GIRL.

329
00:12:44,062 --> 00:12:47,098
♪♪♪

330
00:12:47,098 --> 00:12:48,733
Amanda: MAY I JUST
WORSHIP FOR A SECOND?

331
00:12:48,733 --> 00:12:50,535
- Cynthia: (laughs)
- Amanda: JUST KIDDING.

332
00:12:50,535 --> 00:12:52,404
Cynthia:
YOU'RE SO FUNNY.

333
00:12:52,404 --> 00:12:53,505
- I LIKE YOUR SHOES.
- Amanda: THANK YOU.

334
00:12:53,505 --> 00:12:55,106
I PICKED THEM UP TODAY.

335
00:12:55,106 --> 00:12:57,275
Cynthia: YOU HAD TIME
TO SHOP TODAY? NICE!

336
00:12:57,275 --> 00:12:58,476
YOU'RE CUTE.

337
00:12:58,476 --> 00:13:00,512
SO CAN YOU WALK FOR US?

338
00:13:05,950 --> 00:13:07,419
- Cynthia: SHE CAN'T WALK.
- Man: I KNOW.

339
00:13:09,054 --> 00:13:12,424
Cynthia:
GREAT. PERFECT.

340
00:13:12,424 --> 00:13:13,558
Man: SHE'S GOOD.

341
00:13:13,558 --> 00:13:15,560
Cynthia: OH, NICE!

342
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:18,263
PERFECT, YEAH.

343
00:13:18,263 --> 00:13:18,963
Man: WHOA!

344
00:13:21,933 --> 00:13:23,201
Toccara: THE DRESSES
THAT WERE MY SIZE,

345
00:13:23,201 --> 00:13:25,970
THEY WERE REALLY BIG
AND NO SHAPE AND NO FORM.

346
00:13:25,970 --> 00:13:27,972
I HAVE TO WORK TWICE AS HARD

347
00:13:27,972 --> 00:13:29,641
JUST TO BE ON THE SAME LEVEL
AS THE OTHER GIRLS.

348
00:13:29,641 --> 00:13:32,544
♪♪♪

349
00:13:36,448 --> 00:13:38,149
Marc: ALL RIGHT.

350
00:13:38,149 --> 00:13:40,618
ALL RIGHT, SO STRONG
AND SEXY, NOT TOO FUSSED.

351
00:13:40,618 --> 00:13:41,986
PRETEND WE'RE NOT HERE.

352
00:13:41,986 --> 00:13:45,123
Nicole: TODAY IS LIKE
A 12-HOUR DAY.

353
00:13:45,123 --> 00:13:47,058
I MEAN,
IT'S RIDICULOUSLY TIRING,

354
00:13:47,058 --> 00:13:48,660
AND MODELING IS
VERY DIFFICULT.

355
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:51,196
Marc: JUST KICK YOUR FEET
FORWARD AS YOU WORK.

356
00:13:51,196 --> 00:13:53,131
OOPS.

357
00:13:53,131 --> 00:13:54,499
ALL RIGHT,
LET'S TRY THAT AGAIN.

358
00:13:56,201 --> 00:14:00,071
WHOOPS.
TOCCARA'S A MOVIE STAR.

359
00:14:00,071 --> 00:14:01,573
ALL RIGHT.

360
00:14:03,608 --> 00:14:06,344
OKAY, LET'S TRY TO WALK
WITHOUT TRIPPING THIS TIME.

361
00:14:06,344 --> 00:14:07,612
THAT'S TOO FAST.

362
00:14:07,612 --> 00:14:09,180
Norelle: I'M JUST
CONCENTRATING, LIKE,

363
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:10,648
THE MOST ON NOT FALLING.

364
00:14:10,648 --> 00:14:12,283
Marc: A LITTLE
WOBBLY ON THOSE HEELS.

365
00:14:12,283 --> 00:14:14,719
Norelle: I'M TRYING TO WORK IT
THE BEST THAT I CAN.

366
00:14:16,521 --> 00:14:19,991
Marc: I THINK YOU'RE
TOTALLY READY FOR THE RUNWAY.

367
00:14:19,991 --> 00:14:21,025
GREAT JOB.

368
00:14:23,695 --> 00:14:26,297
I LIKE THAT CONFIDENCE,
GREAT.

369
00:14:26,297 --> 00:14:29,567
I THINK THAT YOUR THIGHS ARE
A LITTLE BIG FOR THIS DRESS.

370
00:14:29,567 --> 00:14:32,203
I'M GONNA HAVE YOU WALK IN IT
WITH THE ZIPPER OPEN.

371
00:14:32,203 --> 00:14:35,573
I THINK THE BIGGEST CONCERN
WITH CASSIE, FOR ME,

372
00:14:35,573 --> 00:14:38,176
WAS THE SIZE OF HER HIPS.

373
00:14:38,176 --> 00:14:39,444
I JUST WANT TO MEASURE
YOUR THIGHS

374
00:14:39,444 --> 00:14:41,012
JUST TO SEE
WHERE WE'RE AT.

375
00:14:41,012 --> 00:14:46,951
NORMALLY WE LIKE ABOUT
NO MORE THAN 35.

376
00:14:46,951 --> 00:14:47,585
Cassie: I THINK
I'M RIGHT AT THAT.

377
00:14:47,585 --> 00:14:49,287
Marc: YOU'RE AT 39.

378
00:14:49,287 --> 00:14:54,192
OKAY, I PREFER
A SMALLER HIP.

379
00:14:54,192 --> 00:14:55,727
Cassie: I DON'T APPRECIATE
THE FACT THAT HE TOLD ME

380
00:14:55,727 --> 00:14:58,062
THAT MY HIPS AND BUTT
WERE TOO BIG

381
00:14:58,062 --> 00:15:00,098
FOR HIS PERSONAL TASTE.

382
00:15:00,098 --> 00:15:04,068
I DON'T NEED TO MODEL
FOR MARC BOUWER.

383
00:15:04,068 --> 00:15:05,236
Man: YOU'VE MADE
HER PERSONALITY EQUAL.

384
00:15:05,236 --> 00:15:06,704
SHE OPENED HER UP TO A 42.

385
00:15:06,704 --> 00:15:09,140
Yaya: AT THE END,
MARC BOUWER IS THE ONE

386
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:12,477
THAT ANNOUNCES TOTAL SUM
SCORES FOR THE DAY.

387
00:15:12,477 --> 00:15:14,112
Marc: OKAY, GIRLS,

388
00:15:14,112 --> 00:15:18,049
STARTING FROM THE LOWEST
TO THE HIGHEST,

389
00:15:18,049 --> 00:15:22,453
NORELLE, YOU SCORED 170.

390
00:15:22,453 --> 00:15:25,623
NICOLE, 178.5.

391
00:15:25,623 --> 00:15:28,726
TOCCARA, 181.

392
00:15:28,726 --> 00:15:32,430
CASSIE, 184.

393
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:34,666
EVA, 188.5.

394
00:15:34,666 --> 00:15:38,536
AMANDA, 188.5.

395
00:15:38,536 --> 00:15:41,272
AND THERE ARE TWO GIRLS THAT
ARE NECK AND NECK IN THIS.

396
00:15:41,272 --> 00:15:44,042
YAYA, 211.

397
00:15:44,042 --> 00:15:47,011
ANN...

398
00:15:47,011 --> 00:15:49,414
207.5.

399
00:15:49,414 --> 00:15:51,082
Girls: (cheering)

400
00:15:51,082 --> 00:15:52,584
Marc: YAYA'S THE WINNER.

401
00:15:52,584 --> 00:15:54,118
YOU'RE GONNA
CHOOSE A FRIEND,

402
00:15:54,118 --> 00:15:56,154
AND YOU'RE GONNA RECEIVE
A RACK OF CLOTHES

403
00:15:56,154 --> 00:15:58,623
FROM ALL THE DESIGNERS
THAT YOU SAW TODAY.

404
00:15:58,623 --> 00:16:00,558
Yaya: NICOLE.

405
00:16:00,558 --> 00:16:02,193
Nicole: THANK YOU.

406
00:16:04,095 --> 00:16:05,530
Norelle: I FELT LIKE
I GAVE MY ALL TODAY

407
00:16:05,530 --> 00:16:07,298
AND DIDN'T GET ANYWHERE.

408
00:16:07,298 --> 00:16:08,499
Eva: CHECK IT,
YOU GIVE YOUR ALL,

409
00:16:08,499 --> 00:16:09,500
AND SOMETIMES IT'S GREAT.

410
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:11,336
Norelle: AND IT'S NOT
GOOD ENOUGH, THOUGH.

411
00:16:11,336 --> 00:16:13,504
IN THE SITUATION THAT WE'RE IN,
I DON'T HAVE THE LUXURY

412
00:16:13,504 --> 00:16:15,173
TO SUCK OR TO BE
AT THE BOTTOM.

413
00:16:15,173 --> 00:16:17,475
BEING LAST, IT MAKES ME
FEEL LIKE, "WHY AM I HERE?

414
00:16:17,475 --> 00:16:19,410
LIKE, POINTLESS."

415
00:16:19,410 --> 00:16:21,613
LIKE, I FEEL LIKE A JOKE.

416
00:16:21,613 --> 00:16:23,615
Eva: YOU HAVE TO MAKE
YOURSELF STRONGER.

417
00:16:23,615 --> 00:16:25,016
YOU STAND UP TALL AND
YOU SAY, "I'M NORELLE."

418
00:16:25,016 --> 00:16:26,117
Amanda: YEAH,
OBSTACLES ARE NOTHING

419
00:16:26,117 --> 00:16:27,518
BUT THINGS TO STEP OFF OF.

420
00:16:33,391 --> 00:16:34,559
Toccara:
I WANNA SEE THIS.

421
00:16:34,559 --> 00:16:36,995
Y'ALL BETTER COME OUT
BEFORE I LOOK AT IT FIRST.

422
00:16:36,995 --> 00:16:39,998
YAYA WINS
THE GO-SEE CHALLENGE,

423
00:16:39,998 --> 00:16:42,533
AND SHE WINS A RACK OF CLOTHES
FROM ALL THE DESIGNERS.

424
00:16:42,533 --> 00:16:44,335
Yaya: FIVE, SIX, SEVEN,
EIGHT AND PICK A LETTER.

425
00:16:44,335 --> 00:16:45,603
(gasping)

426
00:16:45,603 --> 00:16:47,505
Amanda:
ARE THOSE FOR YOU, YAYA?

427
00:16:47,505 --> 00:16:48,573
Yaya: SUGAR MAMA.

428
00:16:48,573 --> 00:16:49,607
Nicole:
NO. THIS IS YAYA'S.

429
00:16:49,607 --> 00:16:50,642
Yaya:
DELICIOUS SUGAR MAMA.

430
00:16:50,642 --> 00:16:52,010
Amanda: OH, THAT IS ADORABLE.

431
00:16:52,010 --> 00:16:53,611
Yaya: "DEAR YAYA, YOU DID
SUCH A GREAT JOB AT THE GO-SEE.

432
00:16:53,611 --> 00:16:55,046
IT WAS A PLEASURE
TO HAVE MET YOU

433
00:16:55,046 --> 00:16:57,248
AND I LOOK FORWARD TO HEARING
A LOT ABOUT YOU IN THE FUTURE.

434
00:16:57,248 --> 00:16:58,316
- LOVE, NANETTE."
- Ann: THAT'S ADORABLE.

435
00:16:58,316 --> 00:17:00,318
LOOK AT YOU.
YOU'RE LIKE, "HEY."

436
00:17:00,318 --> 00:17:02,120
Amanda: PUT IT ON.
PUT THAT ON. PUT IT ON.

437
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:04,222
Toccara: OKAY, I AIN'T
GONNA WATCH NO MORE.

438
00:17:04,222 --> 00:17:05,490
I'M GOING BACK TO BED.

439
00:17:08,526 --> 00:17:11,262
I AM VERY HAPPY FOR YAYA,
AND AT THE SAME TIME,

440
00:17:11,262 --> 00:17:14,232
I WAS GETTIN' NERVOUS AND
SCARED BECAUSE YOU DON'T SEE

441
00:17:14,232 --> 00:17:16,701
A LOT OF BIG GIRLS
IN HIGH FASHION.

442
00:17:16,701 --> 00:17:18,102
Yaya: AW, THIS IS CUTE.

443
00:17:26,577 --> 00:17:29,380
Toccara: I TOTALLY FEEL
A LOT OF PRESSURE

444
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:33,284
BECAUSE I'M HERE
WITH GIRLS WHO ARE ALL THIN

445
00:17:33,284 --> 00:17:36,120
AND I DON'T KNOW HOW TO
COMPETE WITH THEM.

446
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:37,188
COOL THEN.

447
00:17:37,188 --> 00:17:39,123
LET ME GO TRY MY CLOTHES.
I'LL BE BACK.

448
00:17:45,530 --> 00:17:48,199
Norelle: I THINK
I'M NOT DOING GOOD.

449
00:17:48,199 --> 00:17:49,967
Norelle's mom: Well, you're
doing the best that you can.

450
00:17:49,967 --> 00:17:51,235
Norelle: YEAH,
BUT THAT'S NOT GOOD ENOUGH.

451
00:17:51,235 --> 00:17:54,105
AND I FELT GOOD, AND, LIKE,
I WAS THE WORST ONE HERE.

452
00:17:54,105 --> 00:17:57,408
AT FIRST I WAS SO MAD THAT
